<h2>2. The Bullish Engulfing Pattern</h2>
<p>A <strong>bullish engulfing</strong> pattern appears after a downward move. It signals potential reversal upward. It requires exactly <strong>two consecutive bars</strong>:</p>

<div class="candle-grid">
  <div class="candle-wrap">
    <svg class="candle-svg" width="60" height="160" viewBox="0 0 60 160">
      <line x1="30" y1="30" x2="30" y2="60" stroke="#c01c28" stroke-width="2"/>
      <line x1="30" y1="110" x2="30" y2="138" stroke="#c01c28" stroke-width="2"/>
      <rect x="12" y="60" width="36" height="50" fill="#c01c28" rx="2"/>
      <text x="64" y="63" fill="#ccc" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">prev.Open</text>
      <text x="64" y="112" fill="#ccc" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">prev.Close</text>
    </svg>
    <span class="candle-label">Bar N (prev)<br>RED — seller control</span>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size: 2rem; align-self: center; color: #555;">→</div>
  <div class="candle-wrap">
    <svg class="candle-svg" width="60" height="160" viewBox="0 0 60 160">
      <line x1="30" y1="15" x2="30" y2="50" stroke="#26a269" stroke-width="2"/>
      <line x1="30" y1="130" x2="30" y2="148" stroke="#26a269" stroke-width="2"/>
      <rect x="12" y="50" width="36" height="80" fill="#26a269" rx="2"/>
      <text x="64" y="53" fill="#ccc" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">curr.Close ≥ prev.Open</text>
      <text x="64" y="132" fill="#ccc" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">curr.Open ≤ prev.Close</text>
    </svg>
    <span class="candle-label">Bar N+1 (curr)<br>GREEN — engulfs prev</span>
  </div>
  <div style="flex:1; min-width:200px;">
    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;"><strong>Four conditions must all be true:</strong></p>
    <ol style="margin-left:1.2rem; font-size:0.9rem; line-height:2;">
      <li><code>prev.Open &gt; prev.Close</code> — prev is red</li>
      <li><code>curr.Close &gt; curr.Open</code> — curr is green</li>
      <li><code>curr.Open &lt;= prev.Close</code> — opens inside or below prev body</li>
      <li><code>curr.Close &gt;= prev.Open</code> — closes above prev body top</li>
    </ol>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">The current candle's <em>body</em> must fully wrap the previous candle's body. Wicks do not count.</p>
  </div>
</div>

