  <div class="question" data-question>
    <p>A bar has Open=50.00 and Close=50.01. The DOJI_THRESHOLD is 0.0005. Is this a doji?</p>
    <ul class="options">
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="Body = |50.01 - 50.00| = 0.01. Threshold = 0.0005 × 50.01 = 0.025. Since 0.01 < 0.025, it IS a doji.">No — body of 0.01 is large enough.</li>
      <li data-correct="true" data-why="body = 0.01, threshold = 0.0005 × 50.01 ≈ 0.025. Since 0.01 < 0.025, this bar qualifies as a doji and would cause generate_signal to return HOLD.">Yes — body (0.01) is less than 0.05% of price (0.025).</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="DOJI_THRESHOLD is defined once as a module constant. It doesn't need to be passed — _is_doji uses it directly.">Impossible to know without passing the threshold explicitly.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="feedback"></p>
  </div>

  <div class="question" data-question>
    <p>In the paper engine, a BUY signal fires at bar index 47 (the 47th bar). At what price does the trade entry occur?</p>
    <ul class="options">
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="Using Close of bar 47 is lookahead — the bar isn't closed yet when the signal is confirmed at its close. Wait for bar 48.">Bar 47's Close price — use the current bar's last price.</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="Bar 47's Open is the price at the start of the signal bar — but you don't know the bar is an engulfing signal until it closes.">Bar 47's Open price — use the signal bar's first price.</li>
      <li data-correct="true" data-why="The signal is confirmed at bar 47's close, but you can only act on bar 48's open — the first price available after the pattern completes. This eliminates lookahead bias at the execution level.">Bar 48's Open price — the next bar's first available price.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="feedback"></p>
  </div>

