<h2>9. Scenarios — Check Your Understanding</h2>
<p>Work through these mentally:</p>
<ol style="margin-left:1.4rem; line-height:2.5;">
  <li>prev: O=200, C=210 (green). curr: O=215, C=195 (red, opens with gap up). Does curr engulf prev? <em style="color:var(--muted)">(Yes — bearish engulfing. curr.Open=215 ≥ prev.Close=210 ✓, curr.Close=195 ≤ prev.Open=200 ✓)</em></li>
  <li>prev: O=100, C=90 (red). curr: O=88, C=95 (green, closes only partway). Engulfing? <em style="color:var(--muted)">(No — curr.Close=95 &lt; prev.Open=100, so it doesn't reach the top of prev's body)</em></li>
  <li>prev: O=50.00, C=50.001 (essentially flat). DOJI_THRESHOLD=0.0005. Body = 0.001, threshold = 0.025. Doji? <em style="color:var(--muted)">(Yes — 0.001 &lt; 0.025, so generate_signal returns HOLD regardless of curr)</em></li>
  <li>A signal fires at bar 100. The position opens at bar 101's Open. Bar 102 has Low=97 when stop is at 98. Does stop trigger? <em style="color:var(--muted)">(Yes — bar Low ≤ stop price. The engine closes at 98, not 97)</em></li>
</ol>

<script>
// Shuffle quiz options and wire click handlers
function shuffle(arr) {
  for (let i = arr.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
    [arr[i], arr[j]] = [arr[j], arr[i]];
  }
  return arr;
}

let totalQ = 0, answeredQ = 0;
document.querySelectorAll('[data-question]').forEach(q => {
  totalQ++;
  const list = q.querySelector('.options');
  const fb = q.querySelector('.feedback');
  shuffle([...list.children]).forEach(li => list.appendChild(li));
  list.querySelectorAll('li').forEach(li => {
    li.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (q.dataset.answered) return;
      q.dataset.answered = 'true';
      answeredQ++;
      const correct = li.dataset.correct === 'true';
      li.classList.add(correct ? 'correct' : 'wrong');
      if (!correct) {
        list.querySelectorAll('[data-correct="true"]').forEach(r => r.classList.add('correct'));
      }
      fb.style.display = 'block';
      fb.style.color = correct ? 'var(--green)' : 'var(--red)';
      fb.textContent = (correct ? '✓ Correct. ' : '✗ Not quite. ') + li.dataset.why;
      document.getElementById('score-display').textContent =
        `Score: ${document.querySelectorAll('[data-answered]').length} / ${totalQ} answered`;
    });
  });
});
document.getElementById('score-display').textContent = `Score: 0 / ${totalQ} answered`;
</script>

